## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a beginner OTCA path with privacy by design, geohash-based location masking, and per-tenant residency.

## Key Concepts

- Ingest-time privacy and per-tenant opt-in

- Geohash granularity and redaction strategy

- Regional topics and date-partitioned Parquet

- End-to-end testing for privacy, QoS, and data freshness

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for ingest
function ingest(event) {
  // redact precise coords, derive geohash4
  const hash = geohash.encode(event.lat, event.lon, 4);
  const out = {
    tenant_id: event.tenant_id,
    event_type: event.event_type,
    timestamp: event.timestamp,
    geohash4: hash,
    session_id: event.session_id
  };
  publish(out);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate audits for tenants with opt-in vs opt-out?

- How would you monitor latency and privacy violations in production?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical schema evolution, privacy at ingest, and how it affects dashboards.

## Key Concepts
- OTCA streaming, schema evolution, privacy policies, per-tenant isolation
- Schema Registry, Avro/JSON schemas, backward compatibility
- Ingestion pipeline and storage layout (Parquet partitions)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo policy application at ingest
function applyPolicy(tenant, payload){
  const policy = getPolicy(tenant);
  if(policy.redact) redact(payload, policy.fields);
  if(policy.drop) dropFields(payload, policy.fields);
  return payload;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you migrate existing data when a policy changes?
- How would you monitor schema compatibility over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates ability to design data-rights enforcement in OTCA with cross-region flows and immutable stores.

## Key Concepts
- Deletion token propagation
- Tombstone and GC semantics for Kafka
- Immutable storage considerations (Parquet/S3)
- Auditability and legal holds
- Schema-versioning to avoid replay risks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: emit tombstone and propagate deletion token
function deleteTenantData(tenantId){
  emitKafkaTombstone(tenantId);
  purgeDerivedFeatures(tenantId);
  markParquetShardsDeleted(tenantId);
  updateCentralRegistry(tenantId);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test deletion under concurrent deletion requests?
- How would you handle multi-tenant data that migrates regions after deletion?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates designing an OTCA telemetry path for a real-time chat app with multi-region tenants, focusing on privacy at ingestion, data residency, and practical streaming topology.

## Key Concepts
- OTCA tenancy and data residency
- Chat-event schema (message_sent, typing events, read_receipt)
- Privacy at ingestion: redaction and hashing
- Idempotent deduplication and per-tenant rate limits
- Streaming: edge gateway, regional Kafka, Parquet on S3 with tenant/date partitions

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactEvent(e){
  const copy = { ...e };
  copy.user_id_hash = hash(copy.user_id_hash);
  delete copy.personal_message;
  return copy;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify privacy guarantees across tenants during retention cycles?
- What metrics would you surface to validate QoS and latency under load?
